<title>FRANCE: French M3 money supply falls 0.2 pct in April.</title>
<headline>French M3 money supply falls 0.2 pct in April.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-06-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of France gave the following money supply figures.</p>
<p> Money measure  Billions   Monthly change  12-month change</p>
<p>(end-April)    (unadj)	(adjusted)	(unadjusted)</p>
<p>				    April  March	April</p>
<p>    M1	    1,687.1    -1.1    2.8	   2.9</p>
<p>    M2	    3,291.0     0.0    2.0	   6.3</p>
<p>    M3	    5,246.7    -0.2    1.0	  -1.9</p>
<p>    M4	    5,341.0    -0.2    0.9	  -1.9</p>
<p> Investment     2,018.9     1.3    0.9	  15.5</p>
<p> Credit measure	 Billions    month/month	 year/year</p>
<p> (end-Mar )		(unadj)     end-Feb	    end-Mar</p>
<p> Tot. domestic debt   10,965.5	 0.1		  3.0</p>
<p>of which:</p>
<p>  state		    3,623.0	 ---		  7.5</p>
<p>  credits to economy   6,300.5	 0.4		 -1.8</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
